From 44a29a7f4e3f003570e111d676010eacc04dbe5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:12:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: one skip-advice rule for kanban show and
 notices; quota-wall skips offer no pool re-place

PR #1835 review nits (t_01a1d2da4ff64b39, review 5885415248):
1. For a recorded non-ordering skip plus a pool hint, `kanban show` (local_words) replaced the skip advice with
   the pool re-place, while chat notices and ready_hint (_options -> notice_advice -> advice(skip)) kept both.
   One rule now (local_words._skip_advice): the re-place sentence, then the skip's own advice, said once.
   Ordering skips keep the lane's own advice, as before.
2. A pinned_quota_wall skip advised a pool re-place on both local_words branches, dropping "starts on its own
   when that wall resets / re-pin". _pool_could_run (placement_coordination.stranded) never reads the pool
   workers' quota and a re-place keeps the walled pin, so kanban_dispatch_skip.pool_replace_helps() is False for
   that skip: local_words and _pool_sentence (ready_hint, chat-wait and parent-unclaimed notices) drop the
   re-place and keep the quota-wall advice.
3. UNRECORDED_ADVICE and UNRECORDED_POOL_ADVICE share UNRECORDED_FACT.

Proof: 3 new tests RED at bb32212d43 (all 3 fail), GREEN after; the #1835 no-census test moves to an owner_down
skip under the new rule. 27 importer/notice test files: 633 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
